        <headline>Wind Advisory issued September 25 at 2:09AM PDT until September 25 at 5:00PM PDT by NWS Seattle WA</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...West winds 15 to 30 mph with gusts up to 45 mph expected.

* WHERE...Middle Chehalis River Valley, Southern Hood Canal,
Foothills and Valleys of Pierce and Southern King Counties,
Foothills and Valleys of Thurston and Lewis Counties, Lowlands of
Lewis and Southern Thurston Counties, Lowlands of Pierce and
Southern King Counties, Olympia and Southern Puget Sound, and
Willapa and Black Hills.

* WHEN...From 10 AM this morning to 5 PM PDT this afternoon.

* IMPACTS...Gusty winds will blow around unsecured objects. Tree
limbs could be blown down and a few power outages may result.
</description>
        <instruction>Winds this strong can make driving difficult, especially for high
profile vehicles. Use extra caution.</instruction>
